 Possible bias when fitting linear regression with errors in variables using TMB\r\n    </a>\r\n  \r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n    \r\n      <tbody><tr><td style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(46,46,46);font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211)\">\r\n        <span style=\"color:rgb(177,176,176);font-size:15px\">\r\n          DM Gillis &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">astros...@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Jul 20 05:09AM -0700\r\n        </span>\r\n        <br><br>\r\n        I am trying to develop a simple errors in variables (measurement error) <br>\r\nexample using TMB,  by including erros in X as a random variable. It is not <br>\r\nspecified as Random in making the objective function, since I do not want <br>\r\nits effects to be integrated out. The slope returned is an improvement from <br>\r\nthe OLS solution, but the 95% CI falls short or the &quot;true&quot; value (simulated <br>\r\ndata) rather than being centered around it. I have posted details with a <br>\r\nfull code listing on Stack Overflow:<br>\r\n <br>\r\n<a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/76705890/possible-bias-when-fitting-linear-regression-with-errors-in-variables-using-tmb\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://stackoverflow.com/questions/76705890/possible-bias-when-fitting-linear-regression-with-errors-in-variables-using-tmb&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461701631000&amp;usg=AOvVaw26aYZVaUyRQ4PT4Fogp_tU\">https://stackoverflow.com/questions/76705890/possible-bias-when-fitting-linear-regression-with-errors-in-variables-using-tmb</a><br>\r\n <br>\r\nsince my attempt to post it all here was rejected by the server. Any <br>\r\nsuggestions would be appreciated. Thank you for taking thetime to consider <br>\r\nmy problem.<br>\r\n <br>\r\nRegards, Darren<br>\r\n\r\n      </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n  </tbody></table>\r\n  <div style=\"font-size:11px;margi